     1	# Contribution Contract
     2	
     3	Locked by paper-stanford-contribution-locker on 2026-05-30. This file is the
     4	single source of truth for what this paper may and may not claim. Every later agent
     5	(framer, researcher, drafter, every gate) is bound by it. The boundary below may only
     6	be widened by an explicit re-lock routed back to this agent, with the change recorded.
     7	
     8	Lock note: the prior file was a bare TODO stub (no real prior contribution), so this is
     9	a first lock, not a revision of meaningful content. The contribution itself was supplied
    10	pre-decided by the orchestrator and is locked here verbatim in intent, narrowed to one
    11	sentence and bounded against the verified result artifacts. It was NOT expanded.
    12	
    13	## Contribution (one sentence)
    14	
    15	A controlled distribution-shift teardown of a single shipped production driving model
    16	(openpilot v0.9.7 supercombo) shows it fails silently under visual out-of-distribution
    17	input (simultaneous output-head collapse, recurrent-feature freeze, and a non-responsive
    18	uncertainty channel), localizes the failure downstream of the vision encoder, and
    19	demonstrates that a zero-retraining recurrent-feature monitor (E6, the rolling temporal
    20	spread of the 512-D state) detects the collapse about 0.23 blend-units before the outputs
    21	cliff and at about 1% real-driving false-positive rate, where location-based feature-space
    22	OOD scores (Mahalanobis, Relative Mahalanobis, KNN) fail to transfer across real corpora.
    23	
    24	## Target venue and tier
    25	
    26	- Venue: SafeAI @ UAI 2026 workshop (confirmed open) as primary; arXiv preprint
    27	  (CoRL/RSS-style formatting) as the immediate deliverable.
    28	- Tier: workshop.
    29	- Why this tier: the evidence is a single-model (N=1: supercombo v0.9.7) negative finding
    30	  plus a monitor demonstrated offline, with an N=2 real-corpus calibration estimate and
    31	  one extreme OOD axis (CARLA) plus one bounding axis (ImageNet-C); that is exactly a
    32	  strong workshop / preprint contribution, not a main-track generalization result. The
    33	  evidence strength caps the tier; ambition does not raise it.
    34	
    35	## Claim boundary
    36	
    37	### This paper IS allowed to claim
    38	
    39	- A parity-exact reimplementation of openpilot v0.9.7 supercombo inference, verified to
    40	  within +/-0.5 m/s^2 of comma's reference output on 100% of 1159 real-footage frames,
    41	  median absolute delta 0.04 m/s^2 (report/teardown_results.md context; paper_draft.md
    42	  Section 4.1). This is the load-bearing harness-trust claim for the negative result.
    43	- The silent-collapse phenomenon ON THIS ONE MODEL under CARLA-rendered input: 8 of 10
    44	  output heads collapse to under 1% of real-driving temporal activity, the 512-D recurrent
    45	  feature spread drops to about 1e-5 of real, and the predictive-uncertainty heads rise
    46	  only 1.20x to 1.84x with 0% of OOD frames (0 of 220) exceeding the real-driving p95
    47	  (E1/E2/E3, report/teardown_results.md).
    48	- The collapse is a hard cliff on the Subaru alpha-blend axis (E4, transition width 0.015,
    49	  output activity falling 0.9x to 0.1x of real over alpha 0.784 to 0.799), with the cliff
    50	  path being segment-dependent: on the RAM source it is a gradient (width 0.274), so cliff
    51	  headroom cannot be assumed to generalize across segments (E4-RAM, paper_plan.md Section 5).
    52	- The localization: the collapse is downstream of the vision encoder (every encoder stage
    53	  stays at or above real activity across the full sweep), entering at the recurrent
    54	  summarizer VAE-mu bottleneck and the action-block feedback path (E5,
    55	  paper_draft.md Section 5 E5). State this as PARTIAL localization (a VAE-mu/sigma
    56	  ambiguity remains, per report/e5_submodule_results.md).
    57	- E6 detection with early warning: the rolling-spread monitor fires (>50% of frames) at
    58	  alpha=0.550, about 0.23 blend-units before the E4 output cliff at alpha~0.784, with
    59	  AUROC 0.996 [0.992, 1.000] at alpha=1.0 (report/e6_results.md, report/metrics_results.md).
    60	- E6 cross-corpus calibration where the location-based baselines do not transfer: E6 holds
    61	  LOCO mean FPR 1.03% (max 2.07%) across {subaru, ram}, while Mahalanobis, Relative
    62	  Mahalanobis, and KNN-50 each hit 100% LOCO FPR, and PCA-Mahalanobis only reaches 11.91%
    63	  LOCO FPR (still far above 1%) (report/e6_results.md, report/metrics_results.md). State
    64	  this as an N=2 two-fold estimate, not a production FPR.
    65	- The two-way bounded corruption result (E7 + E7 overlay): the silent collapse is
    66	  SIM-SPECIFIC, no ImageNet-C corruption reproduces it (at most 1 of 10 output heads
    67	  collapses on any of 75 corruption-severity cells, versus 7 of 10 under CARLA), and E6 is
    68	  COLLAPSE-SPECIFIC (correctly quiet on the real-frame corruptions the model tolerates,
    69	  with its few firings, frost sev3/sev5, gaussian-noise sev4, impulse-noise sev5, tracking
    70	  a recurrent-feature-spread shift rather than any output collapse; 0 false negatives
    71	  because there is no collapse to miss) (report/e7_results.md, report/e7_overlay_results.md).
    72	- That phantom braking under distribution shift is a known, user-reported failure mode of
    73	  the shipped model, cited ONLY as motivation (commaai issue #20704 / discussion #22212).
    74	
    75	### This paper is NOT allowed to claim
    76	
    77	- Any generalization of the silent-collapse phenomenon or of E6 beyond supercombo v0.9.7
    78	  (N=1 model; no other openpilot version, Tesla, Mobileye, Waymo, or research IL stack
    79	  was tested).
    80	- A statistically meaningful or production-grade false-positive rate for E6 (N=2 real
    81	  corpora; LOCO is a two-fold estimate whose variance is not meaningfully reportable).
    82	- That E6 is a universal or general-purpose OOD detector (E7 shows it is collapse-specific;
    83	  it is near chance on most photometric corruptions).
    84	- That E6 generalizes to non-CARLA corruptions AS A COLLAPSE DETECTOR (no non-CARLA output
    85	  collapse was ever induced, so there is no non-CARLA collapse for E6 to have caught).
    86	- Any on-road, in-stack, or real-robot deployment of E6 (it is demonstrated offline on
    87	  logged, rendered, and corrupted frames only).
    88	- Any causal claim linking this collapse to specific openpilot field incidents beyond
    89	  citing the user-reported phantom-braking issue as motivation.
    90	- That the localization is complete or fully mechanistic (it is partial; a VAE-mu/sigma
    91	  ambiguity remains).
    92	
    93	## Do NOT claim (exclusion list)
    94	
    95	These are the exact tempting sentences a careless drafter would write. Do not write them.
    96	
    97	- "We show that production driving models fail silently under distribution shift."
    98	  (Wrong: N=1, this is supercombo v0.9.7 only; say "a production driving model" and name it.)
    99	- "E6 is a general-purpose / universal OOD detector for driving models."
   100	  (Wrong: E6 is collapse-specific; near chance on most ImageNet-C corruptions, mean AUROC
   101	  0.52 to 0.74 on the photometric/blur families.)
   102	- "E6 generalizes beyond CARLA, detecting OOD on real-world corruptions."
   103	  (Wrong: E6's few corruption firings are decoupled from output collapse; no non-CARLA
   104	  collapse was induced, so there is nothing for E6 to have generalized to as a collapse
   105	  detector.)
   106	- "E6 achieves a 1% false-positive rate in production driving."
   107	  (Wrong: 1.03% is a LOCO two-fold estimate over N=2 corpora, not a production FPR.)
   108	- "E6 beats / outperforms standard OOD baselines."
   109	  (Careful: KNN-50 ties E6 at AUROC 1.000 at alpha=1.0; the real, narrower claim is that
   110	  the location-based baselines FAIL TO TRANSFER across corpora (100% LOCO FPR) while E6
   111	  calibrates. Frame it as transfer/calibration, not raw separation.)
   112	- "We achieve state-of-the-art OOD detection."
   113	  (Wrong: there is no SOTA leaderboard or benchmark ranking here; this is a single-model
   114	  diagnostic with a calibration comparison.)
   115	- "Our monitor can be deployed on the vehicle to prevent phantom braking."
   116	  (Wrong: E6 is offline-only; no on-road, in-stack, or real-time deployment was run, and
   117	  no causal link to field incidents was established.)
   118	- "This explains / is the cause of openpilot's reported phantom braking."
   119	  (Wrong: the field issue is motivation only; no causal claim is supported.)
   120	- "The model fails to perceive simulated scenes." / "The vision encoder fails on sim."
   121	  (Wrong: E5 localizes the collapse DOWNSTREAM of the encoder; the encoder stages stay at
   122	  or above real activity. The failure is in the summarizer/action-block, not perception.)
   123	- "The collapse is a universal cliff." (Wrong: cliff vs gradient is segment-dependent;
   124	  RAM is a gradient with width 0.274 and no early-warning headroom.)
   125	
   126	## Out-of-scope contributions (parked, not this paper)
   127	
   128	- A second, real adverse-weather OOD axis (rain/night/glare comma footage) that actually
   129	  induces a non-CARLA output collapse. The brief and plan flag this as the most
   130	  reviewer-resistant follow-up; it is curation-gated and deferred to an extended version.
   131	  (paper_plan.md Section 3.2, Option B.)
   132	- A MetaDrive (non-CARLA sim) collapse axis. Deferred and de-prioritized due to the known
   133	  bridge confound (commaai issue #31711). (paper_plan.md Section 3.1, Option A.)
   134	- A multi-model / cross-version study (other openpilot versions, other vendors, research IL
   135	  stacks) to test whether silent collapse generalizes. This is the N>1 paper, explicitly
   136	  not this one.
   137	- A third+ real corpus to turn the LOCO estimate into a reportable production FPR with
   138	  variance. Parked; needed before any production-FPR claim.
   139	- An online / in-stack deployment and evaluation of E6 inside the running openpilot stack.
   140	  Parked; this paper is offline-only.
   141	- A complete mechanistic account of the VAE-mu/sigma summarizer bottleneck (resolving the
   142	  remaining localization ambiguity). Parked as future work.
