405:activity ratio of each encoder stage across the alpha sweep. It is not. Every encoder stage stays at or
406:above real activity across the full sweep: at alpha=1 the stem is at 1.43x, stage3 at 2.06x, and the
407:head at 2.14x, and the minimum ratio over all stages and all alpha is about 0.96. No encoder stage ever
408:crosses the 0.5 collapse threshold. The encoder is in fact more active on CARLA than on real input, so
