523:## 6. Limitations
528:**N=1 model.** Every result is on supercombo v0.9.7 alone. No other openpilot version, and no Tesla,
532:the N>1 study this paper does not attempt.
534:**N=2 corpora; LOCO is a two-fold estimate.** The cross-corpus calibration rests on two real corpora.
535:Leave-one-corpus-out at N=2 is a two-fold estimate whose variance is not meaningfully reportable, and the
536:roughly 1% FPR is therefore a calibration estimate, not a production false-positive rate. A third real
537:corpus, at minimum, is needed before any single production FPR can be quoted with an uncertainty.
539:**Monitor scope: collapse-specific and offline-only.** The corruption overlay (Section 5.7) shows the
543:that no non-CARLA output collapse was ever induced, so the monitor was never tested as a collapse detector
544:on anything other than CARLA; real adverse-weather footage (rain, night, glare) that actually induces a
545:non-CARLA collapse remains pending, and is the most reviewer-resistant follow-up.
554:## 7. Conclusion
556:A shipped Level-2 driving model, openpilot v0.9.7 supercombo, shown CARLA-rendered input, collapses to a
557:plausible near-constant and does not raise its own uncertainty: 8 of 10 output heads fall to under 1% of
558:real activity, the recurrent state freezes to about 1e-5 of its real spread, and 0 of 219
559:out-of-distribution frames exceeds the model's real-driving uncertainty p95. A simulation "pass" can
564:second-order statistic, the rolling temporal spread of the 512-D state: one O(d) quantity per forward pass,
565:with no retraining and no architecture change. Calibrated leave-one-corpus-out to about a 1% real-driving
566:FPR (N=2, a two-fold estimate), it separates the collapse at AUROC 0.996 and fires about 0.23 blend-units
568:(Mahalanobis, relative Mahalanobis, KNN) each hit 100% leave-one-corpus-out FPR and fail to transfer across
